%N A398907 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} H(k-1) * binomial(2*k,k)*((zeta(3) - H(k,3)) - (H(2*k) - H(k) - log(2))*(zeta(2) - H(k,2))) / (k * 4^k), where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k), H(k,2) = A007406(k)/A007407(k), and H(k,3) = A007408(k)/A007409(k) are the k-th harmonic number of order 1, 2, and 3, respectively.
%H A398907 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.59, p. 456, eq. (4.194), section 5.59, p. 469, section 6.59, pp. 802-807.
